# Folded into the op-fusion pack by make_fusion_jobs.py from references/upload-p0-jobs/T3-upload-b.env (pack_include, WP0): the one image, the template otherwise as its package wrote it.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/upload-p0 four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the branch and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the
# cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-upload-p0-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the branch (the next2-1 stack plus qwen_device_zeros, qwen_lazy_shard and
# the six upload twins of the production profile, docs/tp4-fabric-upload.md P0 and P1a); substitute it in every template with one command (sed -i 's/tp4-upload-p0-1/<tag>/' *.env).
# The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent (production is down by the owner's choice while it runs).
# T3: the TIMED ENGINE START, flag arm again, round B.
# READ: c2_smoke_check clean, the engine reaches Application startup complete, then python3 scripts/ci/engine_start_phases.py --control <T0 or T2 container log> --flag <this container log> and judge the PAIR: the table's
# 'layers' row is the weights (P1a), 'kv_pool' and 'buffer_pool' the zero buffers (P0), 'total' the engine start. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED and no other engine start or build beside it; record `uptime` before and after:
# the load average is part of the number (the same stack took 2 min 47 s idle and 9 min 43 s under CI load). The weight cache must be warm (A0 filled it), so every load is a hit. Judge every ABAB PAIRED per round, never by unpaired medians.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic-upload
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup
C2_BOX_MINUTES=40
# Knowingly omits concurrent8_steady: without this key c2_serving_job.py refuses the job. The smoke check is unchanged, so the run still ends red on its eight-seat rule; read the logs.
C2_SMOKE_PARTIAL=engine-start timing arm: the engine start is the measurement, one warmup request proves the engine serves, so concurrent8_steady is not run
